Before the Syariah Appeal Court is established under section 6( 1) and the Chief Syar'ie Judge and the panel of Judges of the Syariah Appeal are appointed under sections 8(1) or 9(1) respectively(a)· the Judicial Committee of the Majlis constituted under 44( 1) of the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act be retained with all powers of the Syariah Appeal Court established under section 6( 1) of this Order ;

(b) who holds the office of Chairman of the Judicial the Majlis appointed under section 44( 1) of the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act before the of this Order, shall at the commencement Order be deemed to be the Chief Syar'ie Judge as if he has been appointed under section 8(1) of this

(c) any member of the Judicial Committee of the Majlis under section 44(2) of the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act before the commencement of this Order, the commencement of this Order be deemed to be the panel of Judges of the Syariah Appeal Court as if they have been appointed under section 9(1) of this Order, until their appointments are terminated or the Syariah Appeal Court is whichever is the earlier.
